>
  <p>Hello there! My name is Deni Susanto.</p>

  <p>I'm self-taught in tech, currently focused on DevSecOps. I started learning through my phone in middle school out of pure interest, and got a laptop in my third year of high school, which really accelerated things.</p>

  <p>I was born in Tulungagung, East Java, Indonesia. As a kid I played too many video games on a tablet my brother gave me — until I got my own phone at the start of middle school, and by chance decided I wanted to make my own games instead of just playing them.</p>

  <p>That's actually how I got into programming in the first place. From middle school through high school, my path went from making games, to web development, to cybersecurity — each one opening up a different way of looking at the same problems.</p>

  <p>I still find it fun to look at things from different angles. Right now I'm learning every day: working through PortSwigger labs, TryHackMe, OverTheWire, and CTFs, writing automation scripts, and building personal projects — including, still, the occasional video game.</p>
</Layout>
